0004 — classlink.rs: class constants fetched inside a constant expression
name the class as written.

Inside a constant expression php-src resolves `X::C` with
zend_get_class_constant_ex(class_name, ...), whose errors print class_name
as written ("Undefined constant self::UNKNOWN", "Cannot access private
constant self::X", "Cannot declare self-referencing constant self::BAR"),
and which marks the constant (IS_CONSTANT_VISITED) while evaluating it. The
FETCH_CLASS_CONSTANT opcode instead calls zend_update_class_constant
without marking. op_fetch_class_const now passes the written name (self /
parent / static / the literal) when the current frame is a ConstExpr frame
and evaluates an unevaluated constant unmarked otherwise; class_constant()
keeps its behaviour via the new class_constant_ex(cls, name, shown, mark).

Fixes: ext/reflection/tests/ReflectionClass_toString_004,
ReflectionClassConstant_toString_error; Zend/tests/constants/bug41633_2,
constexpr/constant_expressions_self_referencing_array, array_unpack/classes;
ext/standard/tests/streams/bug77664.

